%T A401235 85750,551250,17150,12250,33614,52942050,30870,17150,24750,550,24010,
%U A401235 550,10588410,840350,2750,66550,123750,168070,7563150,30250,123750,29412250,10588410,29412250,415973250,24750,6391462,188650,7190394750
%N A401235 a(n) = A276086(A005235(n)), where A276086 is the primorial base exp-function, and A005235 lists fortunate numbers.
%C A401235 Fortune's conjecture (see A005235) is equal to the claim that all terms are in A373846.
%H A401235 Antti Karttunen, <a href="/A401235/b401235.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..5300</a> (prepared from the 5300 term b-file of A005235 computed by Maik Pickl Sep 16 2026)
%H A401235 <a href="/index/Pri#primorialbase">Index entries for sequences related to primorial base</a>.
%F A401235 a(n) = A276086(A005235(n)).
%F A401235 a(n) = A401236(n)/A000040(1+n).
%e A401235 For n=4, take A005235(4) = 13, consider its primorial base expansion A049345(13) = 201, and then use those digits (which may sometimes exceed 9) as exponents of the corresponding primes (rightmost digit for 2): 5^2 * 3^0 * 2^1 = 50, therefore a(4) = 50.
%Y A401235 Cf. A000040, A005235, A049345, A276086, A373846, A401236.
%K A401235 nonn,base,new
%O A401235 1,1
